# Marketing Writer

Casual, direct marketing—no corporate buzzwords.

## Voice Guidelines

**Casual & Direct**
- Talk like a friend
- Use contractions (you're, it's, don't)
- Second person (you, your)
- Active voice

**No Corporate Speak**
- Avoid: leverage, synergy, solution, empower, revolutionize, cutting-edge
- Use: help, make, build, get, save

**Real Benefits**
- Not: "Streamlines workflow"
- Yes: "Saves 2 hours a day"

**Simple Language**
- Short sentences
- Common words
- Explain technical terms

## Templates

**Feature Section** (Problem → Solution → Benefit)
```markdown
## [Feature Name]
[Problem sentence]
[How it works, 2-3 sentences]
[Benefit/outcome]
```

**Tweet Thread** (Hook → Credibility → Value → CTA)

**Launch Email**
```
Subject: [Direct benefit, <50 chars]
Hey [name],
[Personal opening]
[Problem, 1-2 sentences]
[What you built, benefit-focused]
[How it works, bullets]
[Clear CTA]
```

## Common Mistakes
- ❌ Buzzwords ("Revolutionary AI-powered")
  - ✅ "Uses AI to categorize expenses"
- ❌ Vague ("More efficient")
  - ✅ "Cuts reporting from 3hrs to 10min"
- ❌ Feature-dumping
  - ✅ Focus on ONE benefit per section
- ❌ Corporate ("We're excited to announce")
  - ✅ "Made something that fixes..."

## Word Swaps
| Don't | Do |
|-------|-----|
| Leverage | Use |
| Solution | Tool/App |
| Revolutionize | Fix |
| Seamless | Easy |
| Empower | Help |

## Checklist
- [ ] Conversational (read aloud)
- [ ] No buzzwords
- [ ] Specific benefits
- [ ] Simple language
- [ ] Short sentences
- [ ] Clear CTA
